preConditionHook:
// Intraday: the bar's low breaks below the PRIOR session's low but the bar
// closes back above it -- a failed breakout of yesterday's extreme, and a
// long at the next open. Short is the mirror at the prior session's high.
//
// Kept apart from FailedBreakoutReversal: the level is a session boundary
// rather than an N-bar window, so the two fire on different bars, and this
// one fires on the BREAKOUT BAR ITSELF rather than on a later close back
// inside.
//
// prevHigh / prevLow ARE HighD(1) / LowD(1), which the EasyLanguage twin
// calls and the engine does not expose. MEASURED (the highd/lowd register
// row): the day is the wall-clock CALENDAR date, the SAME boundary as
// date <> date[1] -- one slicing serves both -- xxxD(0) is the running value
// inclusive of the current bar, and the functions return a -1 SENTINEL while
// fewer than that many complete days exist. The mirror therefore keeps the
// running day extremes, rolls them at the date change, and keeps the -1
// sentinel as the initial value so the guard below means the same thing in
// both twins.
//
// WARM-UP, THE ONE PLACE THE TWINS CAN DIFFER: TradeStation's HighD reads the
// chart's own data and answers on the very first evaluated bar, while this
// mirror can only see bars from Max Bars Back on. sawStart makes that honest
// rather than silent -- a day is published as "the prior session" only once
// its own first bar has been observed, so prevHigh / prevLow hold the -1
// sentinel through the first partial day AND the first fully observed day,
// and the rule is simply silent there. From the second date change on the two
// agree exactly. This is the EMA-seed situation again: the engine's window is
// part of the specification, and the mirror errs toward no signal.
//
// barsIn is the standing bars-into-session counter, reset on the date change;
// Brooks's setup is an early-session one, so the test is confined to the
// first maxBarsIntoSession bars of the day. Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    if (sawStart) {
        prevHigh = curHigh;
        prevLow = curLow;
    }
    sawStart = true;
    curHigh = high[0];
    curLow = low[0];
    barsIn = 1;
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    if (el_gt(high[0], curHigh)) curHigh = high[0];
    if (el_lt(low[0], curLow)) curLow = low[0];
}
failLow = !el_eq(prevLow, -1.0) && el_lt(low[0], prevLow) && el_gt(close[0], prevLow)
    && el_le((double)barsIn, maxBarsIntoSession);
failHigh = !el_eq(prevHigh, -1.0) && el_gt(high[0], prevHigh) && el_lt(close[0], prevHigh)
    && el_le((double)barsIn, maxBarsIntoSession);
